    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262">

                <pb facs="0200" n="192" xml:id="pg192"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.44A15/88: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-05T18:00:00-06:00">December 5, 1939—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:28 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>60. The Foreign Minister informs me that his Government has as yet heard nothing
                    from the British Legation regarding the forthcoming British proposals outlined
                    in the Department’s telegram No. 51, November 15, 5 p.m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
